    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "We can identify the general term in the expansion of $\\left(x+y\\right)^6$ using the Binomial Theorem:\n$$\nT_{r+1} = \\binom{6}{r} x^{6-r} y^{r}\n$$\nTo find the coefficient of the $x^2y^4$ term,\nwe set $6-r=2$ and $r=4$ in the general term to get:\n$$\nT_{4+1} = \\binom{6}{4} x^{6-4} y^{4} = \\binom{6}{4} x^2 y^4\n$$\nNow we compute $\\binom{6}{4}$:\n$$\n\\binom{6}{4} = \\frac{6!}{4!(6-4)!} = \\frac{6!}{4!2!} = \\frac{6 \\cdot 5}{2 \\cdot 1} = 15\n$$\nSo, the coefficient is $\\boxed{15}$.",
